# AEML Governance Platform - Project Rules & Idioms

## 1. Stack & Runtime
- Language: TypeScript 5.7+ (Strict Mode enabled).
- Runtime: Node.js 22 (ESM/CJS hybrid, bundling via esbuild + Vite).
- Client: React 18, Tailwind CSS, Lucide React icons, Recharts for data visualizations.
- Server: Express.js with JSON body parsing and static SPA fallback routing.

## 2. TypeScript & Code Quality
- Never use `any` when a specific interface, generic, or union type is known.
- All domain interfaces must be defined and centralized in `src/types.ts`.
- Always prefer named exports over default exports for utility modules and components.
- Keep components modular: extract sub-components from primary views.

## 3. Server & Architecture Security
- API endpoints must always precede Vite/SPA wildcard static handlers.
- Never expose API keys (such as `GEMINI_API_KEY`) to the browser client; proxy all requests through `/api/*` endpoints.
- Ensure all mutations persist to disk via `server/persistenceAdapter.ts` using safe atomic writes.
- Listen exclusively on host `0.0.0.0` and port `3000` to support container and ingress reverse proxies.

## 4. UI & React Guidelines
- Strictly use Tailwind CSS utility classes; avoid inline styles or standalone `.css` files.
- All icons must be imported directly from `lucide-react`.
- When animating or transitioning views, use `motion` from `motion/react`.
- Support seamless Dark Mode styling using `darkMode` state and Tailwind dark variants.
